  "question": {
    "text": "A small object is placed at the centre of a large evacuated hollow spherical container. Assume the container is maintained at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. At time&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, the temperature of the object is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. The temperature of the object becomes&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>&nbsp;at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>&nbsp;at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. Assume the object and the container to be ideal black bodies. The heat capacity of the object does not depend on temperature. The ratio&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced></math>&nbsp;_________ ."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "9",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0003_1a65b16e78e9.png\" style=\"width: 147px; height: 150px;\" /></p><p>Using Stefan-Boltzmann law,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#963;</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>A</mi><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>B</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>&#8722;</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>S</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8757;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>&#963;</mi><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mtext>consider</mtext><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>also,&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>s</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>&#963;</mi><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munderover><mrow><mo>-</mo><mo>&#8747;</mo></mrow><mn>200</mn><mi>T</mi></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>where</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#963;</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>&#8722;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>200</mn></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;</p><p>For case&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>100</mn></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>&#8722;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>200</mn></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>For case&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>50</mn></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>&#8722;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>200</mn></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Divide&nbsp;equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math> by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>50</mn></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>&#8722;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>200</mn></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>100</mn></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>&#8722;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>200</mn></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p>"
  }
